From c1c5e9a36eae711528c3a1341f05ddd145007223 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michal Frdlik <michaelf.ms@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 11:59:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 18/22] Thylacine Warp vkQuake-arc W-3d: the WSI DIRECT path
 (vn_wsi_thylacine)

Venus swapchains whose images are Thylacine compositor PRESENTABLES
(WARP-WSI-DESIGN section 5): the guest half of the model tapestryd's
img/new landed at W-3c-1, riding mesa's own swapchain machinery.

The surface class is stock VK_EXT_headless_surface -- Thylacine has no
window-system handle, and a headless ICD surface is exactly "a surface
with no intrinsic identity". vn_wsi_init replaces the interface behind
wsi[VK_ICD_WSI_PLATFORM_HEADLESS] with the Thylacine one
(vn_wsi_thylacine.c); wsi_common keeps the entire swapchain state
machine. Only the two designed wsi_image_info hooks are ours:

- create_mem: a MARKED dedicated vkAllocateMemory. The chain-head
  driver-internal pNext (VN_STRUCTURE_TYPE_THYLACINE_WSI_MEMORY_INFO,
  'THLW', stripped in vn_device_memory_alloc before anything is
  encoded) routes the allocation to alloc_simple: venus-side memory,
  NO renderer bo. The memory's ONE vkr blob export (mem->exported is
  one-shot) is deliberately left for the compositor's img/new. That
  one-export rule makes both wrong orders fail loudly rather than
  tear: an eagerly-minted bo consumes the export and registration
  refuses (swapchain creation fails); a later vkMapMemory needs a bo
  whose mint the consumed export refuses (the presentable is
  never-map by design).
- finish_create: vn_device_memory_wait_alloc (host-allocate before
  the registration names mem->base.id -- the V-3b-3c-2b F7 ordering,
  wait_alloc de-static'd for it) then vn_renderer_thylacine_img_new
  with the LINEAR stride vkGetImageSubresourceLayout reported.

The I-40 stage-0 present bracket holds on BOTH paths: venus's own
vtest-class drain (has_external_sync = has_implicit_fencing = false,
so every vn_QueueSubmit* tail runs vn_wsi_fence_wait, which detects
the async-present tid and does the empty-submit + fence + synchronous
wait) AND the vtable queue_present's own wait on the per-image
throttle fence, so the bracket survives VN_PERF=no_async_present.
The present poke (present-to <surface> img <n>, consent-dedup'd; the
surface named by the vn_renderer_thylacine_set_surface +1-encoded
process global) stays DORMANT until the W-3e SDL glue -- a
surfaceless swapchain is a pure headless rotation.

vn_renderer_thylacine grows the img handle family: a 16-slot
img_bitmap (MAX_WARP_IMGS_PER_CTX) under the transport mutex with the
mem family's two-sided invariant, plus vn_thylacine_bo_create_count
(the prove's no-eager-mint witness). warp_client grows warp_img_new /
warp_img_destroy / warp_present_to_img -- the mem family's
three-valued contract with two arms re-derived rather than copied:
E_INVAL keeps the handle (duplicate and validation refusals are
indistinguishable at the client, so the caller keeps its inputs
client-valid and the validation arm unreachable); E_IO resolves via
warp_img_reclaim (the server's clean one-export refusal installs
nothing, but the client cannot distinguish it from a transport EIO
after a commit -- the F9 shape).

meson: the thylacine branch now compiles vn_wsi.c + the new file and
defines VN_USE_WSI_PLATFORM -- every prior build ran the stub inlines.
The define also flips KHR_swapchain and can_sync2 onto
renderer_sync_fd.semaphore_importable, a HOST property queried through
the ring (v3dv answers SYNC_FD importable via vkr's passthrough).

thylacine_prove step 10: probe KHR_swapchain (FAIL, never skip, on
absence); headless surface -> 3-image 640x400 BGRA8 FIFO swapchain;
the bo-create counter's delta across creation must be ZERO with a
NONZERO baseline (the positive control -- a dead counter cannot
satisfy the negative); a GPU clear-to-red INTO presentable 0 +
vkCmdCopyImageToBuffer + pixel-exact readback (the registered memory
is a real, GPU-writable render target); acquire/present x3 through
the async-present path. Witness line "venus-prove: wsi swapchain OK".

Self-audit SA-1 (folded): the create-loop failure path destroyed the
failed image twice -- wsi_create_image's own fail arm already ran
wsi_destroy_image, which does not null the struct's handles; the
cleanup now excludes the failed index (which can never be registered:
finish_create is the last fallible step and sets the flag only on
success).

Alternative considered: a hand-rolled image path (vkCreateImage +
bind + register without wsi_create_image). Rejected -- the
create_mem/finish_create hooks are the designed injection points, and
wants_linear exists precisely to pin the CPU-image config to the
NO_BLIT LINEAR arm; less code and the stock error discipline.

